<subsection xml:id="unit4c-project2">
    <title>Unit 4C Project 2 - Theater Seats</title>
<p>
  Create a program about Theater Seating.  A theater seating chart is implemented as a two-dimensional array of ticket prices, like this:
</p>
<pre>
10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10
10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10
10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10
10	10 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	10 	10
10 	10 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	10 	10
10 	10 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	10 	10
20 	20 	30 	30 	40 	40 	30 	30 	20 	20
20 	30 	30 	40 	50 	50 	40 	30 	30 	20
30 	40 	50 	50 	50 	50 	50 	50 	40 	30
</pre>
<p>
  In main, create a 2D array using the values above.  Write a program that prompts users to pick either a seat (by specifying the row and column) or a price.  Mark sold seats by changing the price to 0.  When a user specifies a seat, make sure it is available.  When a user specifies a price, find any seat with that price.  If a user picks a seat that is not available, notify them as such.  After the user has successfully picked a seat, print out the seat location and price and the updated 2D array.  Use a while loop with a sentinel value to allow the user to pick as many seats as they would like until they indicate they are done.
</p>
<p>
  In main, create a 2D array using the values above.  Write a program that prompts users to pick either a seat (by specifying the row and column) or a price.  Mark sold seats by changing the price to 0.  When a user specifies a seat, make sure it is available.  When a user specifies a price, find any seat with that price.  If a user picks a seat that is not available, notify them as such.  After the user has successfully picked a seat, print out the seat location and price and the updated 2D array.  Use a while loop with a sentinel value to allow the user to pick as many seats as they would like until they indicate they are done.
</p>
<p>
Use the outline below to help you create this program.
</p>

<p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>
        Setup &amp; Initialization: 
        Create a 2D array using an initializer list, initialize a <c>Scanner</c> object, and declare a <c>boolean</c> variable to control the loop.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Main Program Loop: 
        Use a <c>while</c> loop (controlled by the boolean variable) to allow repeated ticket purchases.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>
            Display Seating: 
            Print the 2D array using nested <c>for</c> loops, putting a tab between each entry.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Prompt Purchase Method:
            Ask the user to purchase by price (<c>"p"</c>) or seat location (<c>"s"</c>) and store the input in a <c>String</c>.<line/>
            <em>Note: Use <c>scan.next()</c> instead of <c>scan.nextLine()</c> to avoid Scanner buffering issues when mixing Strings and ints.</em>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Option A — Purchase by Price: 
            Ask for the target price and pass it along with the 2D array to a static method named <c>findPrice()</c>.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p>
                If available: <c>findPrice()</c> updates the seat location to <c>0</c> and returns: <em>"You purchased the seat at row __, column __ for $__"</em> (adjust array 0-indices to 1-based theater numbers).
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>
                If unavailable: Returns <em>"There is no seat available at that price."</em>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Option B — Purchase by Location: 
            Ask for the row and column numbers and pass them along with the 2D array to a static method named <c>findSeat()</c>.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p>
                <title>If available:</title>
                <c>findSeat()</c> updates the seat location to <c>0</c> and returns: <em>"You purchased the seat at row __, column __ for $__"</em>.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>
                <title>If unavailable:</title>
                Returns: <em>"That seat is not available."</em>
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>
                <em>Note: Subtract 1 from the user's row and column inputs to map 1-based seat choices to 0-based array indices.</em>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            <title>Continue or Exit:</title>
            Ask the user if they want to buy another seat (<c>Y</c> or <c>N</c>). If <c>"N"</c>, update the boolean variable to terminate the loop.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <c>findPrice</c> Method:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>
            This static method should take two parameters: the 2D array and the price, and return a String that will be printed in the if statement.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            This method should find the first seat at that price, change that location to 0 to indicate it is now purchased, and return a String in the form: <c>You purchased the seat at row __, column __ for $__</c>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Remember that even though the 2D array starts at row 0, column 0, the theater would start at row 1, column 1.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            If there are no seats left at that price, the method should return the String: <c>There is no seat available at that price.</c>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <c>findSeat</c> Method
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>
            This method should check whether or not the requested seat is available.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p>
                Remember that the user will enter a seat thinking that the first row and column are 1, not 0, so be sure to adjust the values for the 2D array.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            This static method should have three parameters: the 2D array, the row choice, and the column choice, and it should return a String that will be printed.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            If the seat is not available, the method should return the String: <c>That seat is not available.</c>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Otherwise, the method should change that location to 0 to indicate it is now purchased, and return a String in the form: <c>You purchased the seat at row __, column __ for $__</c>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <p>
                Remember to adjust the row and column numbers again.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</p>

<activity label="unit4c-project2-theaterseats">
<statement>
  <p>
  Create a program about Theater Seating.  A theater seating chart is implemented as a two-dimensional array of ticket prices, like this:
</p>
<pre>
10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10
10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10
10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10	10
10	10 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	10 	10
10 	10 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	10 	10
10 	10 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	20 	10 	10
20 	20 	30 	30 	40 	40 	30 	30 	20 	20
20 	30 	30 	40 	50 	50 	40 	30 	30 	20
30 	40 	50 	50 	50 	50 	50 	50 	40 	30
</pre>
<p>
  Use the outline above to help you write your code.
</p>
</statement>
<program interactive="activecode" language="java">
<code>
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

    }
}
</code>
<tests>    
import static org.junit.Assert.*;
import org.junit.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.ArrayList;


public class RunestoneTests extends CodeTestHelper
{
    public RunestoneTests() {
        super("Main", input1.replaceAll(" ", "\n")); // For Book
    }


    private static String input1 = "p 10 Y s 8 2 Y s 8 2 N";
    private static String input2 = "p 10 N";
    private static String input3 = "";


    private int[][] seats = {{10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 10, 10}, {20, 20, 30, 30, 40, 40, 30, 30, 20, 20}, {20, 30, 30, 40, 50, 50, 40, 30, 30, 20}, {30, 40, 50, 50, 50, 50, 50, 50, 40, 30}};
    private String seatsList = "{{10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 10, 10}, {10, 10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 10, 10}, {20, 20, 30, 30, 40, 40, 30, 30, 20, 20}, {20, 30, 30, 40, 50, 50, 40, 30, 30, 20}, {30, 40, 50, 50, 50, 50, 50, 50, 40, 30}};";


    @Test
    public void test01(){
        seatsList = seatsList.replaceAll("},", "},\n");


        String code = getCode();
        code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args)");


        String[] lines = code.split("\n");
        String expected = "int[][]";
        String actual = "";


        for (String line : lines){
            if (line.contains(expected) || (line.contains("{") &amp;&amp; line.contains(","))) {
                actual += line.trim() + "\n";
            }
        }


        expected = "int[][] * = {{...}, ...};\n" + getDescription(seatsList);


        boolean passed = stringMatch(actual, seatsList);


        String incorrect = "";
        if(!passed) {
            incorrect = "\nIncorrect indexes: " + valuesIncorrect(actual.substring(actual.indexOf("{")), seatsList);
        }


        actual = actual.substring(0, 30) + "...\n" + getDescription(actual.substring(actual.indexOf("{"))) + incorrect;


        getResults(expected,actual,"Creates 2D array of seats using initializer list",passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }


    private String valuesIncorrect(String actual, String expect) {
        String result = "";


        String[][] actMatrix = makeMatrix(actual);
        String[][] expMatrix = makeMatrix(expect);


        if (actMatrix.length != expMatrix.length || actMatrix[0].length != expMatrix[0].length) {
            return "Results have different dimensions";
        }


        for (int r = 0; r &lt; actMatrix.length; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c &lt; actMatrix[0].length; c++) {
                if (!actMatrix[r][c].equals(expMatrix[r][c])) {
                    result += "(" + r + ", " + c + ") ";
                }
            }
        }


        return result;
    }


    private void printMatrix(String[][] matrix) {
        for (int r = 0; r &lt; matrix.length; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c &lt; matrix[0].length; c++) {
                System.out.print(matrix[r][c] + "\t");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }


    private String[][] makeMatrix (String initList) {
        String[] lines = initList.split("\n");
        String[][] matrix = new String[lines.length][];


        int i = 0;
        for (String line : lines) {
            line = line.replaceAll("[{},;]","").trim();
            matrix[i] = line.split("\\s");
            i++;
        }
        return matrix;
    }


    private String getDescription(String initList) {
        String[][] matrix = makeMatrix(initList);


        return "2D array of size " + matrix.length + " x " + matrix[0].length;
    }


    @Test
    public void test02(){
        String code = getCode();
        code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args)");


        String[] lines = code.split("\n");
        String expected = "while(";
        String actual = "";


        for (String line : lines){
            if (line.contains(expected)) {
                actual += line.trim() + "\n";
            }
        }


        boolean passed = actual.contains(expected);
        expected = "while(*)";


        getResults(expected,actual,"Uses one while loop",passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }


    @Test
    public void test03(){
        String input1 = "p 10 Y p 10 N";
        String output1 = getMethodOutputWithInput("main", input1.replaceAll(" ", "\n"));


        String input2 = "p 10 N";
        String output2 = getMethodOutputWithInput("main", input2.replaceAll(" ", "\n"));


        int num = output1.length() / output2.length();
        String expected = "Code executes 2 times";
        String actual = "Code executes " + num + " times";


        boolean passed = num == 2;
        getResults(expected,actual,"While loop ends when user enters N (testing using \"p 10 Y p 10 N\" for input)",passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }


    @Test
    public void test04(){
        String code = getCode();
        String method = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[]");
        String expected = "Prints 9 x 10 2d array\nUses nested loops";
        try {


            code = getMethodCode(code, "for(");
            int fors = countOccurences(method, "for(");


            String output = getMethodOutputWithInput("main", input2.replaceAll(" ", "\n"));


            String[] lines = output.split("\n");
            String actual = "";
            String[] matrix = new String[9];
            int i = 0;


            for (String line : lines){
                if (i &lt; 10 &amp;&amp; line.matches("[0-9\\s]+")) {
                    actual += line.trim() + "\n";
                    matrix[i] = actual.trim();
                    i++;
                }
            }


            int rows = -1;
            int cols = -1;


            if (i &gt; 0) {
                rows = matrix.length;
                cols = matrix[0].split("\\s").length;
                actual = "Prints " + rows + " x " + cols + " 2d array\n";
            } else {
                actual = "No matrix printed\n";
            }


            if (fors == 2) {
                actual += "Uses nested for loops";
            } else if (fors &lt; 2) {
                actual += "Not enough for loops";
            } else {
                actual += "Too many for loops";
            }


            boolean passed = rows == 9 &amp;&amp; cols == 10 &amp;&amp; fors == 2;


            getResults(expected,actual,"Prints the 2D array in matrix format using nested for loops (make sure there is a space between the ints)",passed);
            assertTrue(passed);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            getResults(expected,"No matrix printed","Prints the 2D array in matrix format using nested for loops (make sure there is a space between the ints)", false);
            assertTrue(false);
        }
    }


    @Test
    public void test05(){
        String code = getCode();
        code = getMethodCode(code, "main(String[] args)");


        String[] lines = code.split("\n");
        String expected = "Scanner";
        String actual = "";


        for (String line : lines){
            if (line.contains(expected)) {
                actual += line.trim() + "\n";
            } else if (line.contains(".next") &amp;&amp; line.contains("()")) {
                actual += line.trim() + "\n";
            }
        }


        expected = "Scanner * = new Scanner (System.in);\nint * = *.nextInt();\nString * = *.next();\nString * = *.nextLine();";
        boolean created = stringMatch(actual, "= new Scanner(System.in);");
        boolean nextInt = stringMatch(actual, ".nextInt()");
        boolean next = stringMatch(actual, ".next()") || stringMatch(actual, ".nextLine()");


        boolean passed = created &amp;&amp; nextInt &amp;&amp; next;


        getResults(expected,actual,"Uses Scanner to scan in Strings and ints",passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }


    @Test
    public void test06(){
        String code = getCode();


        String[] lines = code.split("\n");
        String expected = "findPrice(int[][]";
        String actual = "";


        for (String line : lines){
            if (stringMatch(line, expected)) {
                actual += line + "\n";
            }
        }


        boolean passed = actual.contains("static") &amp;&amp; stringMatch(actual, "int[][]") &amp;&amp; stringMatch(actual, ", int") &amp;&amp; actual.contains("String");


        String expect = "public static String findPrice(int[][] *, int *)";


        getResults(expect,actual,"Correct header for findPrice method",passed);
        assertTrue(passed);
    }


